IrisUI — references and third-party notices

This file records visual references and resource licenses for IrisUI's native modules and the local frontend prototype in tmp/frontend_design/.

Design references

- User-supplied Endfield screenshots and endfieldui-like-irisui-design.svg: composition and interaction reference; screenshots are not included in the frontend asset bundle.
- Endfield Design Skill: https://github.com/Statrue/endfield-design-skill . Installed separately into omp; used as design guidance. Its MIT license is reproduced below.
- IrisMenus local Endfield-like prototype: existing theme and component conventions.
- Endfield UI 1.2.1 React components and design guidance: https://icaruszezen.github.io/endfield-ui/design/overview/ and https://icaruszezen.github.io/endfield-ui/design/surfaces/game-ui/ . The prototype uses the library's controls, compact tabs, fullscreen SideRail navigation, rows, tags, progress, tooltips, corner brackets and TickRing. Fullscreen uses a 2D character studio with a side-profile echo, projected shadow, fading perspective lines flowing from near to far, character-color circles and right-side angular fields. The right-edge rail has tall items, bottom-centered icons and white current-page selection. Page changes stage character motion before panel reveal and staggered information; reduced motion displays the settled layout. Psychic levels are synthetic preview values, not read from a game save.
- Radius UI: user-supplied screenshots inform the Minimum and Normal inspector densities. No Radius UI binaries, source or assets were read, decompiled, copied or included in this prototype. IrisUI is not presented as an extension of Radius UI. Minimum shows a portrait, name and mood; Normal adds tabs and details. Neither mode nor fullscreen provides a draft action. Switching characters preserves the current mode and page.
- The six portrait SVGs and shared side-profile echo SVG are original simplified illustrations made for this prototype. Names, biographies, attributes and colony values are synthetic preview data, not real game records.
- Native Framework and Inspector reuse IrisMenus drawing controls and glyphs under their existing licenses; no Endfield or Radius UI artwork is bundled. Pawn portraits are rendered by RimWorld's PortraitsCache at runtime. The two module Preview.png images are original geometric artwork generated for IrisUI.


